1
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:02,400
You win!

2
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:08,820
I wonder what it's like in
the Everlasting Stratum?

3
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,686
Well, it's an unconquered place of darkness
at the lowest level of this dungeon.

4
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,480
There's a big open area at the start.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:17,900
Then a valley.

6
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,336
One so deep you can't see the bottom.

7
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,797
Past that, there are three straight paths.

8
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,500
And that's it. Really?

9
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,015
It gets even weirder.

10
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,917
Of the three, only the path that's
on the right has ever been bested.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,717
A certain hunter walked down
that path for an entire year.

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,897
It seemed to stretch onward
in a straight line forever.

13
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:38,509
Until eventually he
encountered a dead end.

14
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:43,106
And that, they say, is why it's
called the Everlasting Stratum.

15
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:46,337
It feels like I could die of
boredom just thinking about it.

16
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,250
Pidgey, too.

17
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:48,679
That sounds awful.

18
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:51,477
He must have had an iron
will and super sensible

19
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:54,077
shoes to walk a dark
path for a whole year.

20
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:57,984
I hear it took the hunter another
year just to make it back home.

21
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,937
He never so much as saw a
plant, much less a monster.

22
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:05,397
He would have normally starved to death,
but it seems his blessing got him through.

23
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:09,217
Whoa, you think maybe that's why
Captain Kerioyl wants Boxo so bad?

24
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,130
It makes sense.

25
00:01:10,213 --> 00:01:12,777
We know Sulream has the
blessing of transference,

26
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:14,957
but it only works if she's been there.

27
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,460
So they progress, warp back, and restock,

28
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:21,517
repeating the cycle over and over again
whenever they run out of food and stuff.

29
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,777
That sounds like a brutal existence.

30
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:25,380
If they had yours truly,

31
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,277
they'd be drowning in packaged food,

32
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,557
and I could store their
stuff in my coin lockers.

33
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,405
It doesn't sound amazing, but
we'll suck it up and try our best.

34
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:37,297
I bet even a year will fly by in no
time if we're together, you know?

35
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:38,420
That's so true!

36
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:41,014
I'll be happy as long as I'm with Foxo!

37
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:44,737
Foxo here will keep our bellies
nice and full, so no worries there!

38
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:45,700
Pity agrees.

39
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,038
It'll all work out.

40
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,847
I'm starting to get excited.

41
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,334
But what about wheels?

42
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:54,597
Guess we'll have to rustle up a
team of Unasusu to pull a wagon.

43
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:58,092
Too bad Kiko Yu and Botan on
a round to speed up our trip.

44
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:01,062
The time sink will be our
biggest sticking point.

45
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:02,360
Oh, snap!

46
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:06,132
Speaking of points, I pwned
that mid-ranked shark general.

47
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:08,580
I got honor and over a million points!

48
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:10,090
Ka-ching!

49
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,560
I have 2,370,000!

50
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,917
I'm so close to 3 mil I
can practically smell it!

51
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,647
Which means your boy, Boxo, is this close
to knowing the glories of rank three!

52
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:33,544
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul!

53
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:35,217
In this new world of wonders,

54
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:38,817
I travel to and fro on the back of
my super strong partner, Llamas!

55
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,880
The name's Boxo! Hello there!

56
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,720
That means yes, by the way!

57
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:46,917
I can't give...

58
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,257
This is mine, too You can't give...

59
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,617
...or I can give...

60
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,000
I can't give...

61
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:57,060
Look, look, look I can't
tell him the only thing!

62
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,240
Keep the effort of mini go

63
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:02,157
I can't give...

64
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:05,157
I can't give... I can't give...

65
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,057
I don't think... I don't know...

66
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,920
I can't give...

67
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,117
Don't sue me...

68
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,030
Don't sue me...

69
00:03:12,113 --> 00:03:14,217
I don't want to...

70
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,157
I don't want to...

71
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,977
Get it, take it.

72
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:19,920
I gather that on the world.

73
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,460
I know, so now!

74
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:25,700
You'll be there. Yeah, it's all!

75
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,117
I know, like you.

76
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,400
The light of the stars.

77
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:33,757
If you are here enough?

78
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,781
I want to dream.

79
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,297
That's what it is.

80
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:41,677
I love that you have.

81
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:44,620
I love you.

82
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,757
Master, I shall accompany
you on your journey.

83
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,397
It doesn't matter where you're going.

84
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,077
I would follow you off a cliff.

85
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:00,877
I will join your mission as well.

86
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:04,901
A long journey lends itself to
introspection, which feeds the soul.

87
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:08,897
Unrelated, but long treks are
also treacherous on footwear.

88
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:12,257
We have no choice but to bring a
mountain of spare shoes with us.

89
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:13,170
But worry not.

90
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:17,473
I will dispose of any worn-out pairs
once they're too odorless and filthy.

91
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,260
Anyway, we're going with Master Boxo.

92
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:23,337
That should give us an
overwhelming advantage in

93
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:25,497
our attempt to conquer
the Everlasting Stratum.

94
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:27,177
What could possibly go wrong?

95
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:28,957
You still can't afford to be careless.

96
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:29,980
Yes, yes.

97
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,307
Hey, something wrong, Heavy?

98
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,619
A thought, though I hate to say it.

99
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,657
I imagine the Netherlord
won't be in favor of our trip.

100
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:38,570
Surely not.

101
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:42,797
In fact, there's a strong chance he'll
attempt to sabotage us along the way.

102
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,710
Too true.

103
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:45,670
Director!

104
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:46,730
Sorry, sir,

105
00:04:46,813 --> 00:04:50,177
but I just received word that Pinky
General Kylings has broken out of prison.

106
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:51,090
She escaped?

107
00:04:51,173 --> 00:04:54,977
That goth, five-finger general we
nabbed in the Dark Forest Stratum.

108
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:58,001
Pretty sure she's one of
the Netherlord's baddies.

109
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,513
Did the guards survive?

110
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:01,277
All of those guards were put to sleep,

111
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,417
but thankfully they're
not in any mortal danger.

112
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,330
That's good.

113
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,897
Now tell me what happened.

114
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:09,977
We discovered they were sleeping when it
came time for the scheduled shift change.

115
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,137
Unfortunately, she had already vanished.

116
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:13,985
Her cell was completely empty.

117
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:16,357
A blade had sliced through her bars.

118
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:20,337
They were made of a special alloy that
was designed to block her blessing.

119
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:23,857
You're saying someone with a
flair for martial arts did it.

120
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:26,440
Yumite, is such a thing even possible?

121
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,940
Well, of course it's possible.

122
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,997
I could do the same thing
myself if I wanted to.

123
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,360
You're a scary woman.

124
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:37,100
Whoever broke her out is
immensely talented. Director!

125
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:38,477
There's trouble brewing.

126
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:42,137
A hunter returned to our village after
an expedition, bringing a warning.

127
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,137
There's a whole horde of monsters coming.

128
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:45,050
How many?

129
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,200
That's the thing.

130
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:48,520
He said there were at least 500.

131
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,980
Talk about deja vu.

132
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:56,117
The village is still recovering from
the last time this trope happened.

133
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:59,612
Coyowing's escape just got
slapped down the priority list.

134
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:01,460
Form change!

135
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:08,252
That's a horde all right, and
it's hornier than last time.

136
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,880
Yeah, it's not looking good.

137
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:14,777
Those three types would
normally be fighting each other,

138
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:16,566
but they're after us instead.

139
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,075
Blame the Netherlord.

140
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:22,689
I guess this means he's dead set against
us going to the Everlasting Stratum.

141
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,340
Thank you, Boxo.

142
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:28,617
Having you here in times of crisis
certainly makes things much easier.

143
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:30,417
Thanks for all the cool stuff, Boxo.

144
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,597
You're a lifesaver.

145
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,020
I love this towel.

146
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:37,140
We help each other very much.

147
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:40,024
It's good to hear you say that.

148
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:45,217
After all, we're currently housing a large
number of evacuees from other strata.

149
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:48,417
Your kindness will be rewarded later
when you get the coins you're owed.

150
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,680
I give you my word.

151
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:51,060
Hello there.

152
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,228
Now's a good time to
suck up on projectiles.

153
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:56,397
Grab some arrows and throwing knives.

154
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,740
We also offer weapon and armor repair.

155
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:02,637
Thanks to the stinky crisis we're
in, everything's free of charge.

156
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:05,426
Take what you need and
please don't hold back.

157
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,653
I see I'm not the only one hard at work.

158
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:13,857
That's so sweet of you
to hand out weapons.

159
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:17,297
It's pretty extravagant even
for you to not charge anything.

160
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,300
Simple logic.

161
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:23,188
To quote the timeless wisdom of my father,
sometimes the best gain is to lose.

162
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,597
Now's the perfect chance to
spend some good PR for our brand.

163
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:30,856
Fortunately, I was well-prepared and
already stocked up far in advance.

164
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,617
She's just saying that.

165
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,437
They obviously bought
up all those weapons.

166
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,317
Out of concern for us lowly villagers.

167
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,817
Yeah, I think so too.

168
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:40,860
Hello there!

169
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,337
They're still over a kilometer away.

170
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,697
Weird, they're not getting any closer?

171
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:49,260
Are they stalling?

172
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:52,028
Or amassing their forces
for one big attack?

173
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,360
I'm exhausted. Good morning.

174
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:58,177
Great, guard duty's over!

175
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:59,697
See you later, Boxo.

176
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:01,597
We're gonna go get some shut-eye now.

177
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,497
Try not to push yourself too hard.

178
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:04,410
Yes.

179
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:07,460
We're together, at least till tonight.

180
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:08,617
You're a trooper.

181
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:11,437
Please promise to take a break
should exhaustion overwhelm you.

182
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,800
Thank you very much.

183
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,657
I wonder when our fierce
foes will begin their march.

184
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:19,980
Do you think maybe
they're not going to come?

185
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:23,077
Perhaps we should get this party started.

186
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:26,631
But then we're toast if it
turns out to be a fiendish trap.

187
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:31,177
Should we continue waiting
or launch the first attack?

188
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,260
Or is there an even better option?

189
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:36,377
I'd like your unfiltered
opinions on the matter.

190
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:39,417
If you want a hot take, I got
one ready and waiting for ya!

191
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,397
Let's go pulverize some monsters!

192
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,637
But we're all here talking
about our feelings!

193
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,777
The Monster Horde is
getting bigger and badder!

194
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,637
If we choose to bring the fight to them,

195
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:50,217
we must prepare ourselves
for heavy casualties.

196
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,130
Hold up!

197
00:08:51,213 --> 00:08:52,357
Instead of lots of us dying,

198
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,517
can't we wipe some of them
out with a small strike team?

199
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:57,520
Not dying is at least
worth a try. That said,

200
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,777
I think it would be most
effective to chip away at

201
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:02,757
their numbers by unleashing
some powerful ranged attacks.

202
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,940
Hmm, I know where this is going.

203
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:08,077
If you're in the market for
wholesale destruction magic,

204
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:10,101
I'd be more than happy to oblige.

205
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,030
Simmer down.

206
00:09:11,113 --> 00:09:13,138
Try not to get carried away, Gramps.

207
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:14,090
Brilliant.

208
00:09:14,173 --> 00:09:17,957
We'll prepare a wagon for the strike
team as well as the detachment of guards.

209
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:22,137
If things don't go our way, the team
will immediately retreat to safety.

210
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:25,420
By team, he means this grab
bag of named characters.

211
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:29,879
Be careful, and don't forget to come
running back if things go south.

212
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,632
Don't do anything crazy.

213
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,331
We'll be safe, I promise.

214
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:36,637
And we'll turn tail and run if
things get too dangerous out there.

215
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,000
Well, it'll win.

216
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,440
Who's that box?

217
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:50,477
Say, Gramps, don't you think we
should already be in range by now?

218
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,880
Right you are.

219
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:56,394
Director and Lamas, could you
please park us over there?

220
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,720
Hoxie, Shui, prepare to counterattack.

221
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,400
I'm ready and waiting.

222
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,240
Let's do this already.

223
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:07,000
La imps.

224
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,680
Need something, Boxo?

225
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:11,080
Oh, imp, ma 'i. Huh?

226
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,928
You want me to do what now?

227
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,336
Can you repeat that?

228
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,797
Oh, imp, ma 'i, off the air.

229
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,897
So you really want me to toss
you up and flip you around?

230
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:22,877
Meaning your bottom would be on top?

231
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,180
Yes, yes.

232
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:30,680
Now I'm locked and loaded.

233
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:33,697
I don't really get it, but
if you're sure about this...

234
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:37,160
All right, I hope you like
the wind in your eyes!

235
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,760
Now it's my turn!

236
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:43,360
Concrete foundation blocks ready!

237
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:46,137
Toss up with E.

238
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:49,260
Oh, so that's the reason
you're upside down.

239
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,780
Let's do this!

240
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,980
Did you see that? It worked!

241
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,300
Yes, again.

242
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,746
We'll make use of this
opportunity to retreat.

243
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,234
Long as stay up there.

244
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,157
Keep using whatever Boxo
gives you to keep them at bay.

245
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,070
All righty.

246
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,737
Pity, lighten the wagon.

247
00:11:15,820 --> 00:11:19,500
As for Shui and Hoxie, feel
free to fire away. Sure thing.

248
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:31,917
It's time for

249
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,120
Plan B as unfair.

250
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:43,557
If I had to guess, I'd say
the monsters are probably.

251
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,037
Being controlled by a skull ring,

252
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:49,238
Which means they can only follow
simple orders like attack or retreat.

253
